  "label": "Religious Dogma and Its Role in Social Discourse",
  "description": "Religious dogma refers to authoritative teachings or doctrines that are considered binding and unquestionable within a religious tradition. The top text represents a specific form of religious dogma that uses fear of eternal punishment to enforce belief. The meme's intent to juxtapose this with a statement about child abuse may be intended to critique or satirize the use of religious dogma to justify or explain social issues, or to highlight the absurdity of such extreme beliefs.",
